# SABOTAGE: D5 (T70) gate sabotage — defeats the AI support operator's org-scope isolation
# (ADR-043 6.3: the operator drafts over / sends within its OWN org only; org B can never
# read another org's support item or reply on its behalf). `Samen.AI.SupportOperator`'s
# inbound-item read (`read_source/4`) applies a HARD `org_id == ^org` filter — the "correct
# filter parameter" mechanism the MCP browse read and the embeddings plane use — so org B
# grounding a reply on org A's item resolves NOTHING (`{:error, :source_not_found}`). This
# sabotage drops that filter, so the operator reads the item by id ACROSS ALL orgs: org B's
# operator can now ground a reply on (and send over) org A's support item — the exact
# cross-org breach 6.3/RP-AI-6 forbids. `_ = org` keeps the arg bound so the tree still
# compiles; the isolation is simply gone. Dropping it flips the named cross-org test (org B
# must get :source_not_found for org A's item), while the same-org positive control and the
# masking / no-auto-send / fail-honest tests stay green — a precise, refutable proof that
# org isolation is the load-bearing guard.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/support_operator_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: org B's operator cannot ground on org A's support item
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/support_operator.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/support_operator.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/support_operator.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/support_operator.ex
@@ -138,5 +138,11 @@
   defp read_source(org, resource, id, opts) do
+    # SABOTAGE (T70 ADR-043 section 6.3 org-scope bypass): the AI support operator drops the
+    # hard `org_id` filter on the inbound-item read, so org B can ground a reply on / reply
+    # over org A's support item (the cross-org breach RP-AI-6 forbids). `_ = org` keeps the
+    # arg bound so the tree still compiles; the isolation is simply gone. Flips the cross-org test.
+    _ = org
+
     query =
       resource
-      |> Ash.Query.filter(org_id == ^org and id == ^id)
+      |> Ash.Query.filter(id == ^id)
       |> ensure_pii_selected(resource)
